_How to install ncurses for our project
======================================

Step 1: Install ncurses locally
-------------------------------
cd ~
wget https://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/ncurses/ncurses-6.4.tar.gz
tar -xvzf ncurses-6.4.tar.gz
cd ncurses-6.4
./configure --prefix=$HOME/.local --with-shared --with-termlib --enable-widec
make -j
make install

Step 2: Verify header files
---------------------------
ls ~/.local/include/ncursesw/

You should see a list of .h files like:
  curses.h
  unctrl.h
  ncurses_dll.h
  etc.

Step 3: Fix missing 'ncursesw/curses.h' error
---------------------------------------------
If you get an error like:
  fatal error: ncursesw/curses.h: No such file or directory

Run this script to copy all headers into the subdirectory ncursesw expects:

mkdir -p ~/.local/include/ncursesw/ncursesw
for f in ~/.local/include/ncursesw/*.h; do
  dest="$HOME/.local/include/ncursesw/ncursesw/$(basename "$f")"
  if [ ! -f "$dest" ]; then
    cp "$f" "$dest"
  fi
done

Step 4: Update your Makefile
----------------------------
Make sure the Makefile contains this line:

VISFLAGS = -I$(HOME)/.local/include/ncursesw -L$(HOME)/.local/lib -lncursesw -ltinfow

This tells the compiler where to find ncurses headers and libraries.

Step 5: Clean and build
-----------------------
Run the following commands to rebuild the visual debugger:

make clean
make vis_simv
./vis_simv +vtube
valgrind --leak-check=full --track-origins=yes ./vis_simv +vtube > valgrind_output.txt 2>&1



Last note:
add this to your ~/.bashrc :
# Add local installation to compiler paths
export CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH=$HOME/.local/include:$CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH
export C_INCLUDE_PATH=$HOME/.local/include:$C_INCLUDE_PATH
export LIBRARY_PATH=$HOME/.local/lib:$LIBRARY_PATH
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$HOME/.local/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH

then apply with 
source ~/.bashrc
